  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM_SPEC_CV_CV_OP_DATA_TMP_HANDLER",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h",
    "description": "Use-after-free due to stale zval pointer in ASSIGN_DIM handler when user error handling mutates the target CV ($a) during dimension assignment. The handler caches object_ptr/orig_object_ptr = EX_VAR(op1) and later continues to use/dtor values based on that state, but an error path (undefined index/offset conversion in this PoC) invokes set_error_handler(), which sets $GLOBALS['a']=null and destroys the previously allocated array. Subsequent refcount decrement via zval_ptr_dtor_nogc()/zval_delref_p hits freed zend_array memory (observed in zend_gc_delref). Crash manifests in JIT trace execution but root bug is missing revalidation/liveness protection in this VM ASSIGN_DIM opcode handler.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires ASSIGN_DIM opcodes on a CV array variable that can emit a warning/notice mid-operation (e.g., undefined $c used as dimension), with a user error handler that re-enters and overwrites/frees the same CV ($a). Data flow: fuzzer script executes `$a[$c]...` patterns; warning invokes error handler; handler sets global $a to null, freeing prior array allocated in earlier ASSIGN_DIM; execution resumes in ASSIGN_DIM/JIT path and decrefs stale zval/array pointer, causing UAF."
  },
